// HMZC LTD's official digital stamp — requested directly: "include this
// stamp to all certificate, and invoice, this is supposed to be the
// digital stamp of HMZC." Processed from the original scanned stamp
// (a JPEG with a solid white background) into a transparent PNG —
// pixel alpha set from brightness (near-white -> transparent, dark ink
// -> opaque) — so it can sit directly over a signature and still let
// it show through, the way a real ink stamp validating a signature
// would, rather than covering it with a white rectangle. Embedded as a
// data URI, same pattern as logo.ts, so it needs no bundler asset
// config to work directly in an <img> tag.
//
// Resized from the original 488x155 scan down to 327x104 — the
// stamp only ever renders at a 52px CSS height (SignBox's overlay),
// so the original was roughly 3x larger than any real display size
// ever needs; this keeps it comfortably crisp at up to 2x that for
// high-DPI print while cutting its base64 payload from ~154KB to
// ~72KB. Requested directly, reviewing why a multi-section
// certificate's Paged.js pagination pass (PagedPreview.tsx) was
// taking excessively long: this stamp is embedded once per
// certificate section (every SignatureGrid includes one), so on a
// 4-section certificate the original size alone accounted for over
// 600KB of duplicated image data in the HTML Paged.js has to lay out.
export const HMZC_STAMP_DATA_URI =
  "data:image/png;base64,";
